backend/drm: run multi-GPU test commits for real

A GPU that copies buffers into its own skipped every test commit: the
buffer under test can't be scanned out before it is copied. So no test ever
failed there, and a compositor that looks for another configuration when a
test fails, as sway's output configuration does, never did. A configuration
the kernel then rejects, such as too much bandwidth for two 4K displays on
a dock, left every output of the GPU off.

A test needs a buffer of the GPU's own in the right size and format, not
the copy in it: take the next swapchain buffer, without copying into it,
and run the atomic test with it.

diff --git a/backend/drm/drm.c b/backend/drm/drm.c
index ff169477..827c9a23 100644
